  "how_introduced": "Yes. The first commit that introduced the buggy costaking unbonding logic is 2bd9585607bd7b1c0905d21b92bcdb6d4c03bf36, an AI-attributed backport commit with a Copilot co-author trailer, and that commit directly added the flawed `if !isFpActiveInPrevSet || !isFpActiveInCurrSet` guard that leaves phantom stake behind when a finality provider becomes inactive during BTC unbonding.",
