        "agent_verdicts": [
          {
            "model": "gpt-5.4",
            "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
            "reasoning": "The fix changes `x/costaking/keeper/hooks_finality.go` so `AfterBtcDelegationUnbonded` returns early only when the FP was not active in the previous set; before the fix it returned early whenever the FP was inactive in the current set too. Pickaxe shows 2bd95856 is the first commit to add both `AfterBtcDelegationUnbonded` and the exact vulnerable conditional `if !isFpActiveInPrevSet || !isFpActiveInCurrSet`, and blame on the vulnerable lines points to this same commit. The same commit also had the now-reverted rationale about avoiding 'double subtraction', but `x/finality/keeper/power_dist_change.go` already processed BTC-delegation hooks before FP-removal hooks and `x/incentive/keeper/reward_tracker_store.go` already made `IterateBTCDelegationSatsUpdated` account for pending events, so the FP-removal hook would subtract only the updated remaining active sats. As a result, when an unbond causes an FP to leave the active set, the unbonded sats are never subtracted from the costaker tracker, creating the phantom stake fixed later.",
            "confidence": 0.95,
            "tool_calls_made": 47,
            "steps_completed": 0,
            "evidence": []
          }
        ]
      },
